Below is a **minimal, ready‑to‑run** Discord‑bot dashboard.  
It’s split into three files – *index.html*, *styles.css* and *app.js* – so you can drop them into a folder (or a GitHub repo) and open **index.html** in the browser.

> **What it does**  
> 1. Shows a login button that redirects the user to Discord’s OAuth2 flow.  
> 2. After the OAuth redirect returns a `code` query‑parameter, the script exchanges it for an access token (you’ll need a tiny back‑end endpoint for that – see the comment).  
> 3. With the token it fetches the bot’s **guild list**, **bot status**, and a **command list** (all placeholders you’ll replace with real endpoints).  
> 4. Renders everything in a clean, responsive UI using only vanilla CSS/JS (no heavy frameworks, so it stays lightweight).

